TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES	TAG_PRESTIGE_CLASSES			Dragon Disciples	It is known that certain dragons can take humanoid form and even have humanoid lovers. Sometimes a child is born of this union, and every child of that child unto the thousandth generation claims a bit of draconic blood, be it ever so small. Usually, little comes of it, though mighty sorcerers occasionally attribute their arcane prowess to draconic heritage. For some, however, draconic blood beckons irresistibly. These characters become dragon disciples, who use their magical power as a catalyst to ignite their dragon blood, realizing its fullest potential.Dragon disciples favor the sorcerer class, but bards are not unknown among their ranks. As they progress, their skin thickens into scales, they grow claws and fangs, learn to breathe energy like their draconic forebears, and at last sprout wings and become half-dragons.Hit Die: d12Requirements:To qualify to become a dragon disciple, a character must fulfill all the following criteria.  Race: Any nondragon (all playable races qualify).  Skills: Knowledge (arcana) 8 ranks. Temple+ uses the single Knowledge skill.  Languages: Draconic. Languages are not modelled in ToEE, so this is always met.  Spellcasting: Ability to cast arcane spells without preparation (for example as a ~sorcerer~[TAG_SORCERERS] or ~bard~[TAG_BARDS]).Base Attack and Base Save Bonuses: see ~table~[TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_TABLES]Class Skills: ~Concentration~[TAG_CONCENTRATION], ~Diplomacy~[TAG_DIPLOMACY], Escape Artist, ~Gather Information~[TAG_GATHER_INFORMATION], Knowledge, ~Listen~[TAG_LISTEN], ~Search~[TAG_SEARCH], ~Spellcraft~[TAG_SPELLCRAFT], ~Spot~[TAG_SPOT], Alchemy, Craft, ProfessionSkill Points at Each Level: 2 + Int modifierClass Features:Level 1: Natural armor +1, bonus spell, draconic heritageLevel 2: Claws and bite, Str +2, bonus spellLevel 3: Breath weapon (2d8), bonus spellLevel 4: Natural armor +2, Str +2Level 5: Blindsense 30 ft., bonus spellLevel 6: Con +2, bonus spellLevel 7: Natural armor +3, breath weapon (4d8), bonus spellLevel 8: Int +2Level 9: Wings, bonus spellLevel 10: Blindsense 60 ft., breath weapon (6d8), dragon apotheosis[CMD_CHILDREN]
TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_TABLES	TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES			Dragon Disciple Base Attack & Base Save Bonuses	Level   ~BAB~[TAG_LEVEL_BONUSES]   ~Fort.~[TAG_FORTITUDE]   ~Reflex~[TAG_REFLEX]   ~Will~[TAG_WILL]  1         +0      +2        +0        +2  2         +1      +3        +0        +3  3         +2      +3        +1        +3  4         +3      +4        +1        +4  5         +3      +4        +1        +4  6         +4      +5        +2        +5  7         +5      +5        +2        +5  8         +6      +6        +2        +6  9         +6      +6        +3        +6 10         +7      +7        +3        +7
TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_GRANTED_PROFICIENCIES	TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES			Dragon Disciple Weapon and Armor Proficiency	Dragon disciples gain no proficiency with any weapon or armor.
TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_DRACONIC_HERITAGE	TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES			Dragon Disciple Draconic Heritage	At 1st level, a dragon disciple chooses the variety of dragon in his bloodline from the Class radial menu: black, blue, green, red, white, brass, bronze, copper, gold or silver. The choice is permanent. It sets the energy type of his breath weapon (acid, electricity, fire or cold) and of the energy immunity granted by dragon apotheosis.
TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_BONUS_SPELLS	TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES			Dragon Disciple Bonus Spells	Dragon disciples gain bonus spells as they gain levels in this prestige class. A dragon disciple gains one bonus spell at each of 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 5th, 6th, 7th and 9th level. These are extra spells per day for his spontaneous arcane spellcasting class (such as sorcerer or bard), added to the highest spell level he can currently cast. Dragon disciple levels do not otherwise advance spellcasting (caster level and spells known are unchanged).
TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_NATURAL_ARMOR_INCREASE	TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES			Dragon Disciple Natural Armor Increase	At 1st, 4th, and 7th level, a dragon disciple gains an increase to the character's existing natural armor (if any): +1 at 1st level, +2 at 4th and +3 at 7th. At 10th level (dragon apotheosis) the increase becomes +4. As his skin thickens, a dragon disciple takes on more and more of his progenitor's physical aspect.
TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_CLAWS_AND_BITE	TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES			Dragon Disciple Claws and Bite	At 2nd level, a dragon disciple gains two claw attacks (1d4 each; 1d3 if Small, 1d6 if Large) and a bite attack (1d6; 1d4 if Small, 1d8 if Large).When unarmed, the claws and bite replace unarmed strikes. When wielding weapons, they can still be used as secondary natural attacks (-5 to hit, half Strength bonus to damage); each claw needs a free hand. A buckler, or the Prefer One Handed Wield option with a one-handed weapon, leaves a claw hand free.
TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_ABILITY_BOOST	TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES			Dragon Disciple Ability Boost	As a dragon disciple gains levels, his ability scores increase: Str +2 at 2nd level, Str +2 at 4th, Con +2 at 6th and Int +2 at 8th. Dragon apotheosis adds Str +4 and Cha +2 at 10th level.
TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_BREATH_WEAPON	TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES			Dragon Disciple Breath Weapon	At 3rd level, a dragon disciple gains a minor breath weapon. Once per day, as a standard action from the Class radial menu, he breathes a 30-foot cone of energy of his heritage's type: 2d8 damage, rising to 4d8 at 7th level and 6d8 at 10th. A Reflex save (DC 10 + dragon disciple level + Con modifier) halves the damage.Temple+: varieties that breathe a line in the SRD (black, blue, brass, bronze, copper) also use a cone.
TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_BLINDSENSE	TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES			Dragon Disciple Blindsense	At 5th level, the dragon disciple gains blindsense out to 30 feet, rising to 60 feet at 10th level. Using his other senses, he notices things he cannot see: creatures within range can be noticed and targeted even if they are invisible or in darkness.As blindsense (not blindsight), concealment and invisibility miss chances still apply against such creatures.
TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_WINGS	TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES			Dragon Disciple Wings	At 9th level, a dragon disciple grows a pair of draconic wings.Temple+: the wings are cosmetic only, since ToEE has no flight.
TAG_CLASS_FEATURES_DRAGON_DISCIPLES_DRAGON_APOTHEOSIS	TAG_DRAGON_DISCIPLES			Dragon Disciple Dragon Apotheosis	At 10th level, a dragon disciple takes on the half-dragon template. His natural armor increase becomes +4, he gains Str +4 and Cha +2, and he becomes immune to sleep and paralysis effects and to the energy type of his draconic heritage.Temple+: darkvision and low-light vision are not modelled, and the creature type does not change to dragon.
